--- body ---
## Context

The recall estimate of M3a rests on a known-item list built before the
first round, from outside the search channel frame, by an agent or session
that takes no part in the searches, and sealed by its hash. Normative text:
`docs/jetp-collection.md` § 6 (known items and the recall estimate), § 5
condition 3 (at least 36 of 40), § 12 item 1, § 13; accepted spec v1, tag
`jetp-spec-v1`.

Blocked by [[1877]]: the list is drawn from outside the declared frame and
never from the declared secondary trackers, so both must be declared first.

**Independence.** Whoever builds this list takes no part in the M3a rounds
and does not see the round log; those who search never see the list.
Whoever works this ticket is therefore barred from the campaign.

## Ambiguities in the spec (recorded, not resolved here)

1. **Where `known-items` physically lives.** Collection § 6 keeps the list
   outside the repository, sealed by its hash, until the freeze; the storage
   target `known-items` ([[1871]]) is a ledger table, i.e. in the
   repository. The reading assumed here is *seal then reveal*: before round 1
   only the hash (and the item count) is committed, in the round log; the
   list itself is kept off the repository (a private location the searchers
   cannot read) and committed into `known-items` at the freeze, where the
   hash is checked. Needs confirmation by the author or a spec amendment.
2. **What triggers the freeze.** Collection § 11 freezes the register "when
   the author accepts the recall estimate and the unreachable list"; § 12
   has the author accept the whole collection report. Whether the freeze
   follows acceptance of the two items or of the report is open; it matters
   only if the author accepts one and asks for changes to the other.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] At least 40 items across the four countries, each identified well enough to decide whether a held document is it, drawn from academic and grey-literature reference lists and named experts, none from the declared trackers
- [ ] Built in a session that takes no part in the searches, stated with the session and model
- [ ] The file's SHA-256 and item count are committed (round log or its placeholder) before the first round; the list itself is not readable by the searchers
- [ ] Ambiguity 1 is answered by the author or by a spec amendment before the list is stored
